    {
        "id": "12",
        "stageName": "Satirist",
        "realName": "Carl W. Jones",
        "parish": "St. George's",
        "dateOfInterview": "2026-07-16",
        "tentId": "nvp",
        "photo": "/images/carnival/calypso-artists/artist_1784340266_7646.jpg",
        "videos": [
            "kVqppwno-ok"
        ],
        "shortBio": "",
        "q1": "“Well, actually, I am from... Tempe I grew up in St. George's, from  a Trinidadian father... I was following up calypso since as a teen, in primary school  days.  Listening the Trinidadian calypsonians like Sparrow, Lord Kitchener and Grenadians like old calypsonians  Mighty Hurricane , Mighty Slim... And from then forward, I got a love for calypso... one of my grandparents played... So he taught me music when I was little too... I was inspired by the Director... playing keyboard...”",
        "q2": "“I was following up calypso since... primary school... listen to calypso, Capello, Lord Kitchener, the legendary... Mighty Hurricane, Mighty Slim... I could go on and on. And from then forward, I got a love for calypso... I remember that teenager, then we were little transistor radios... We listen to our calypso king, Mantissa... So... my grandparents... taught me music when I was little too... I was inspired by the keyboard...”",
        "q3": "Calypso is a raw kind of culture. Calypso serves as a platform to address social issues, political issues, and everyday happenings in Grenada (and worldwide).",
        "q4": "“Well, somebody tell me that, 'Why don't you sing one yourself?'... I have a calypso voice... that voice that comes is clarity... and the lyrics and things like that... Not so much fans over there... a raw kind of approach... Grenadian calypso... social issue, political issue... You sing it in song, basically.”",
        "q5": "Four Sundays ago in Spice Basket with my song roots. I didn't know I could sing until people told me.",
        "q6": "Everyone want to do soca , so calypso is struggling but I want to keep it alive.",
        "q7": "“Well, humor, serious lyrics... I'm full of surprises basically... you'll be the judge.”"
    },
