        "shortBio": "make different from the original\r\n\r\nSour Serpent, who took the Mary Monarch title in 2019, turned in a strong showing at the national calypso monarch competition, racking up 519 points over the two rounds.\r\n\r\nHe opened with \"Two Wrongs Make a Right,\" a number that tackled the unresolved standoff between the Keith Mitchell government and Teachers and Public Officers over unpaid pension and gratuity benefits.\r\n\r\nHe followed with \"Call Buju,\" a sharp piece of satire that called out the community and local businesses for overlooking homegrown calypsonians while lavishing attention on international acts like Jamaican reggae star Buju Banton.\r\n\r\nHis songs for 2026 include: Wanted Men, Last Resort",
